+We also assessed code availability, licensing, documentation, and dependencies. Of the 45 projects, 42 link to a code repository; \cref{tab:licenses} tallies license status per project. Explicit licenses are overwhelmingly permissive (19 MIT, 4 Apache-2.0); 12 projects provide no license file, and 5 link to repositories that were private or removed when checked in November 2026. Of the 37 repositories still public, 34 have a README, but only 23 declare their dependencies in a standard file such as requirements.txt, environment.yml, or pyproject.toml, and only 3 have been updated since January 2025; per-project details are in ESI Table S2. Most outputs are therefore reusable starting points rather than maintained tools~\cite{nolte_what_2020}. The tabulation scripts are available in the hackathon repository (see Data availability).
 
